The 90.13% accuracy looks strong in isolation, but the macro-F1 and low sensitivity for the S class show that performance is not equally strong across arrhythmia classes. A high overall accuracy can conceal poor minority-class detection.

What to do: show the confusion matrix, per-class precision and recall, macro-F1, the majority-class baseline, and the exact split protocol next to the headline result. Explain the failure modes and what you would improve next.

For latency, report the hardware, inference runtime, input preparation, and measurement method. Keep the 155.4 KB quantization result if you can reproduce it. Do not imply that this research prototype is clinically validated or ready to diagnose patients.
